# Exactly the owner-only paths of .bosun/risk.toml: every owner-class rule (R-gov, R-ci,
# R-secrets, R-deps), re-rooted under bosun's code root `bosun/` as risk-check does, and bosun's
# critical floor (CRITICAL_PATHS and APPROVAL_CODE_PATHS in bosun/src/core/risk.rs), where no
# delegate approves, and bosun's quorum trust root (QUORUM_CODE_FILES, D-022).
# bosun/tests/governance_owners.rs pins the parity both ways: every such glob has a line here
# and every line maps to one. Code owner review is not required by the ruleset;
# .bosun/risk.toml decides who approves, this file routes the review requests.
#
# CODEOWNERS is case-sensitive, risk-check matches in any case: a name the rules write in lower
# case (`**/agents.md`) is listed in lower case and in its usual spelling (`AGENTS.md`).
# Every glob of the quorum trust root (TRUST_ROOT in bosun/src/core/risk.rs, a rule plus the
# check bosun/tests/trust_root_inputs.rs: `.claude/**` and `.mcp.json` at any depth, and every file
# a trust-root workflow, hook, SessionStart script or secret-holding job reads or executes) has a
# line here, and bosun/tests/governance_owners.rs fails when one is missing or a line maps to none.
# Delegate or two-verdict paths outside the floor are not listed: R-gate and R-ci-review. Under
# quorum (D-022) bosun's quorum trust root is the owner's too (QUORUM_CODE_FILES in
# bosun/src/core/approve.rs, TRUST_ROOT in bosun/src/core/risk.rs), so the folders it compiles in, `bosun/channel/` and `bosun/profiles/`,
# and `bosun/build.rs` are listed here as well.

